# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# This repository is cloned on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites text
# files to CRLF on checkout. For a shell script that is fatal rather than cosmetic: bash
# reads `set -euo pipefail<CR>` and reports `set: pipefail: invalid option name`, so
# `poe docs` (which runs `bash scripts/docs.sh preview`) fails before it does anything.
# Git Bash happens to tolerate it; PowerShell's bash does not, so the failure looks
# shell-specific and unrelated to line endings.
*.sh text eol=lf
